      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The test verifies that `fillExtraField` throws `ZipException` when given an invalid negative offset. I'll improve it with descriptive names and a clear test comment explaining the scenario.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated names (`byteArray0`, `x000A_NTFS0`) with intent-revealing names (`twoByteData`, `ntfsField`, `negativeOffset`, `length`, `isCentralDirectory`) and adds a brief comment explaining that the test verifies wrapping of `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` into `ZipException` when a negative offset is supplied."
